<p>The United States has imposed sanctions on Rwanda’s military and senior Rwandan commanders, accusing them of supporting the M23 rebel movement in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo and of undercutting a peace agreement brokered by President Trump’s administration. US officials said Rwanda’s forces are actively backing M23 and called for the immediate withdrawal of Rwandan troops, weapons, and equipment from eastern Congo — a mineral-rich region where fighting has intensified and displacement has grown. Rwanda’s government rejected the move as “one-sided,” saying it misrepresents the conflict and unfairly targets only one party to the U.S.-brokered peace effort that Kigali refers to as the Washington Accords. The sanctions also add new strain to US-Rwanda ties just as Washington says it is trying to rebuild momentum behind the December 2025 peace treaty signed by Rwanda and Congo’s leaders in Washington.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GwxdBSxese2QGgliiHqKVjE6INkKxlqsRv4m0Q8GIDNQ4kbwhbRdBl-zmQf_RAZ1kagqUwpjYN4UO4A7UsO3AcoLXPKzt6A8UO1WCPQ8cXg5owG_5XfeFYw4OvgrDumbvaA2BOO7DlEQ3ZpNVw1bhJToLndhVi2mr55owDVnURFu1e9ABJYSByGE1wTs8fvLvkgWUCznNpwiQ72It49GV4smrx0' alt='President Trump, President Paul Kagame of Rwanda, and President Felix Tshisekedi of DR Congo at a December 2025 signing ceremony in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who was hit: The measures targeted Rwanda’s army chief of staff, the chief defense staff, and two other senior generals, according to the Treasury announcement described by Semafor.</li><li>US rationale: The US Treasury accused Rwanda of supporting, training, and fighting alongside M23, and said the group is responsible for human rights abuses and a mass displacement crisis in eastern Congo.</li><li>Rwanda’s long-denied role: Semafor said the sanctions directly challenge Rwanda’s long-standing denials that it is providing military support to M23.</li><li>Policy backstory: Semafor reported the administration had tabled sanctions in January after private pressure from Sen. Lindsey Graham, who argued penalties could alienate Rwanda after a call with Kagame.</li><li>Ground situation: Semafor reported M23 has seized major cities, including Goma and Bukavu.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Rwanda government: Kigali rejected the sanctions as “one-sided,” saying they target only one party and distort or misrepresent the facts of the conflict in eastern DR Congo. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202603030072.html'>The New Times (via AllAfrica)</a>)</li><li>US Treasury Department: Treasury said Rwanda’s military is “actively supporting, training, and fighting” alongside M23, and linked the alleged support to access to “mineral-rich areas of eastern DRC.” (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/02/2026/trump-sanctions-rwandas-army-brass-over-drc-conflict'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/us-sanctions-rwandas-defense-force-support-m23-rebels-130688538'>US sanctions Rwanda&#x27;s defense force over support for M23 rebels in Congo</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/02/world/africa/rwanda-sanctions-trump-peace-m23.html'>U.S. Slaps Sanctions on Rwanda, Saying It Sabotaged Trump Peace Deal</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202603030072.html'>Rwanda: Govt Backs RDF Defensive Posture Amidst &#x27;One-Sided&#x27; Sanctions By U.S.</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/02/2026/trump-sanctions-rwandas-army-brass-over-drc-conflict'>US sanctions Rwanda’s top army officers over DR Congo conflict</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-imposes-sanctions-on-rwanda-defense-force'>US imposes sanctions on Rwanda military over east Congo fighting</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/03/us-slaps-sanctions-on-rwanda-military-over-dr-congo-violation_